BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (Delayed allocation postpones physical block assignment until writeback, allowing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (multiblock allocator to choose larger contiguous runs. This reduces immediate fragmentation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (while creating recovery obligations around data that has not yet been placed on the disk.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (Group locality, preallocation and free-space summaries guide the allocator. Physical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (contiguity is a policy goal rather than a structural promise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Directories reference inodes through variable-length records. For larger directories, HTree) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (hashed indexing reduces search cost; inline data and indexed-directory features change) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (exact record locations. Inodes hold ownership, mode, timestamps, size, flags and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (mapping root. Extents, block-size selection and 64-bit feature flags must be interpreted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (consistently across metadata and allocation operations.) Tj ET
